```java
import org.slf4j.Logger;
import org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;

public class OrderService {
    // One logger per class, named after the class
    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(OrderService.class);

    public void processOrder(long orderId) {
        log.trace("Entering processOrder, orderId={}", orderId);   // finest detail
        log.debug("Loading order from DB, orderId={}", orderId);    // dev diagnostics
        Order order = findOrder(orderId);
        log.info("Processing order {} for customer {}", orderId, order.customerId()); // business event
        if (order.total() > 10_000) {
            log.warn("Large order {} exceeds threshold: {}", orderId, order.total()); // handled surprise
        }
        try {
            charge(order);
        } catch (PaymentException e) {
            log.error("Payment failed for order {}", orderId, e); // real failure + stack trace
            throw e;
        }
    }
}
```

With the logger set to INFO, the `trace` and `debug` lines never print — but the same code shows them the moment you lower the threshold to DEBUG.

```java
try {
    paymentGateway.charge(order);
} catch (CardDeclinedException e) {
    // Expected business outcome — the user will try another card
    log.info("Card declined for order {}: {}", order.id(), e.reasonCode());
} catch (GatewayTimeoutException e) {
    // Unexpected but we recovered via retry
    log.warn("Gateway slow for order {}, retrying", order.id());
} catch (GatewayDownException e) {
    // System failure — the order cannot be placed
    log.error("Payment gateway unavailable for order {}", order.id(), e);
    throw e;
}
```

Three exceptions, three very different levels — because the *consequence* differs, not because they are all 'errors'.

```java
// Noise: logs every iteration at INFO, no context
for (Item i : cart.items()) {
    log.info("processing item"); // floods logs, says nothing useful
}

// Signal: one leveled, contextual line per meaningful event
log.debug("Pricing {} items for cart {}", cart.size(), cart.id()); // dev detail
log.info("Order {} placed: {} items, total {}",
         order.id(), order.size(), order.total());                 // business event w/ IDs
```

The second style is searchable, correlatable by `order.id()`, and stays quiet at production INFO level.

