```java
try {
    user = login(email, password);
} catch (BadCredentialsException e) {
    log.info("Failed login attempt for {}", email); // expected, not an error
}

try {
    inventory.reserve(order); // calls a downstream service
} catch (TransientException e) {
    log.warn("Inventory slow, retrying order {}", order.id()); // handled, request continues
} catch (ServiceDownException e) {
    log.error("Inventory unavailable, order {} failed", order.id(), e); // real failure
    throw e;
}
```

Same try/catch shape — the level is chosen by whether the user's request ultimately succeeded.
